{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1499606-of-owls-and-worms-a-vampiric-ecology-head-canon","id":1499606,"title":"Of Owls And Worms: A Vampiric Ecology Head-Canon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-13T21:24:35-08:00","id":1499606,"title":"Of Owls And Worms: A Vampiric Ecology Head-Canon","content":"Hey all, Korogra here! How have you been? So I had been reading the 2e Daeva clan book and had reached the Alu segment when a thought occurred to me: Do Strix prey on the Alu? Knowing what I know about the Owls and how vindictive they are.. I could easily see them as having a bit of a rivalry with the soul eating worms. After all.. the Alu kinda infringe on their territory- being ephemeral vampiric body snatchers and all.. and I could see the very notion of their En symbiotes really rubbing the Strix the wrong way- how DARE these little slugs try to one-up them! <br /> <br /> And then there is the fact that Strix who are powerful enough are able to translate themselves into Twilight.. I like the idea that they will go out of their way to hunt down and devour any Alu they can find.. acting as a sort of \u201cnatural\u201d predator.<br /> <br /> The Alu for their part are pretty much helpless in their base state.. but once they find a Draugr or a Vampire host? Ohh ho ho.. well that\u2019s when they turn the tables- I like to think they are able to sniff out Strix- that ability to detect vampires who have committed diablerie also can work on the Owls as well.. and they will use their new bodies to get payback whenever possible\u2026 ironically being some of best Strix Hunters besides the Strix themselves and the Khaibit\u2026 leading to some pretty vicious little \u201cshadow\u201d wars between these two ethereal vampire species.<br /> <br /> But what do you think? I\u2019d love to hear your thoughts on this idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T05:27:37-08:00","id":1499641,"title":"","content":"Must admit i'm not familiar with the 2e Daeva clan book's take on the Alu - whom i only vaguely remember from the En segment in Ancient Bloodlines - but speaking of vampires and worms or serpents....<br /> <br /> - In <i>Requiem to Rome</i> the undead whom modern kindred know as Nosferatu were called <b>Vermes </b>(worms).<br /> <br /> - One of the origin stories for the <i>Nosferatu </i>in the <i>clanbook </i>speaks of the <b>Brothers Worm</b> coterie, who delved into the dark heart of the earth and ate the immaculate slime <b>of the writhing god</b> that lived there.<br /> <br /> - That tale also dovetails in that being's description considerably with the <b>Zmai </b>in <i>Predators </i>(from WtF).<br /> <br /> - <i>Ancient Mysteries</i> and <i>Ancient Bloodlines</i> speak of the wicked Sta-Au speak of the mysterious Land of Worms that is a major part of their mythology and criteria for picking havens.<br /> <br /> - Incidentally <i>Ancient Mysteries</i>' section on the Land of Worms mentions in its Theories, in the context of the cipher-riddled journal of the Nosferatu Victor Blackcloud, who disappeared within the Land and seems to have come to believe that the Land is a sort of staging ground for the apocalyptic emergence of the <b>Helminth</b>, massive all-consuming worms served by cryptic ghosts from an Underworld beneath all else, (from Summoners', the section on Numbers Stations) and that he himself was infested with worms through his tie to the land.<br /> <br /> - The Sta-Au are also indirectly referenced in <i>Nosferatu </i>and <i>Nightstalkers </i>(from HtV) through reports and snippets on the tale of the <b>Worm Pipe</b>, a legendary native american artifact with the power to ressurect the dead, though at a price for both the user and returned both.<br /> <br /> - In <i>Mythologies </i>one may find the <b>Sons of the Serpent</b> subchapter, one of several early dips on the subject of origins of vampires - and the powers obtained by some who follow them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those are the bits and pieces that come to mind and i could track down but it's probably far from complete, hope they are useful and fun to play with along with your own ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-14-2022, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T18:20:09-08:00","id":1499705,"title":"","content":"Those are all fun things, and clearly show that vampirism isn\u2019t strictly limited to humans or Strix. They don\u2019t seem to have any true connections to the Alu though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T21:37:34-08:00","id":1499718,"title":"","content":"Can an Alu take a Khaibit as host? Or a non-kindred vampire, like one of the beings in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Night_Horrors:_The_Wicked_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">Wicked Dead</a>?<br /> <br /> And speaking of those beings, a little idea just crossed my mind about one of them - what if the double lives of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Aswang\" target=\"_blank\">Aswang</a> were wholly or in part the fruit of some form of possession/symbiosis akin to either Strix or Alu but still its own thing in a number of ways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-15-2022, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T11:18:09-08:00","id":1499768,"title":"","content":"The Khaibit would probably refuse any deal, Obtenebration gives them the ability to render themselves immune to possession already, and the idea of allying with a soul eating abomination probably isn\u2019t something most with jive with. But technically yes, a Khaibit can become an En.<br /> <br /> And the vampire has to either be able to commit Diablerie, or is a Draugr that can\u2019t resist the Alu. Not a lot of non-kindred vampires seem to be able to commit Diablerie, though it\u2019s possible the Alu can give them that ability. Short answer is: unclear, but maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-15T15:16:03-08:00","id":1499790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1499606-of-owls-and-worms-a-vampiric-ecology-head-canon?p=1499768#post1499768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Khaibit would probably refuse any deal, Obtenebration gives them the ability to render themselves immune to possession already, and the idea of allying with a soul eating abomination probably isn\u2019t something most with jive with. But technically yes, a Khaibit can become an En.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a Khaibit could turn Draugr and then become an En - that could make for a pretty unpleasant package indeed, i guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1499606-of-owls-and-worms-a-vampiric-ecology-head-canon?p=1499768#post1499768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the vampire has to either be able to commit Diablerie, or is a Draugr that can\u2019t resist the Alu. Not a lot of non-kindred vampires seem to be able to commit Diablerie, though it\u2019s possible the Alu can give them that ability. Short answer is: unclear, but maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a pretty good question indeed, though what i meant was more along the lines of &quot;<i>could the Aswang's peculiar sort of double life, where it acts and behaves like a normal person during daylight hours, not to mention might be unaware of its supernatural/nocturnal half, the sign of something akin to Strix or Alu possession</i>?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T16:03:12-08:00","id":1500666,"title":"","content":"About the Strix and the Alu - don't know if they would be really antagonistic toward each other or if it's a trick of the mind from a &quot;birds x worms&quot; imagery tempting us to see things in that way.<br /> <br /> For one the Alu are, afaik, a kindred-specific phenomenon/parasite/critter/whatever - the same is definitely not true about the Strix, that may possess a variety of other bodies, human, animal, living, dead as they can inhabit a vampire. It's simply a matter that the disciplines and other natural powers of the kindred make them both an annoyance (due to their powers and tendency to use them enforce some form of Masquerade leading to them trying to put a lid on more blatant supernatural shenanigans) and most tempting targets (due to the remarkable resiliance coming from those same powers).<br /> <br /> Theoretically some parallels do exist and one could speak of a degree of competition for similar niches, but the major differences matter too - the Alu's possession, parasitism or symbiosis whichever you prefer to define as, is basically an one-time deal: once the association is made it can't be undone until destruction. The Strix can wear or discard bodies, kindred or not, like so many suits stolen from a random shop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-18-2023, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T12:17:22-08:00","id":1500756,"title":"","content":"I think that while the Alu possibly might not really regard the Strix as a competitor\u2026 the Birds are vindictive, spiteful assholes who like to bully anything for fun. I could see them as seeing these things as fun to antagonize, if nothing less lol.<br /> <br /> but that is a very fair way to look at it, and is a pretty good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T14:31:21-08:00","id":1500773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1499606-of-owls-and-worms-a-vampiric-ecology-head-canon?p=1500756#post1500756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that while the Alu possibly might not really regard the Strix as a competitor\u2026 the Birds are vindictive, spiteful assholes who like to bully anything for fun. I could see them as seeing these things as fun to antagonize, if nothing less lol.<br /> <br /> but that is a very fair way to look at it, and is a pretty good point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's the point - as you said, Birds are <i>vindictive</i>, spiteful assholes. The Alu don't seem particularly geared on their own to really antagonize and attract much attention from the Strix, not to mention in some ways they kind of <i>help</i> in making vampires more like the Strix prefer them to be. I can just as easily see them exploiting/&quot;helping&quot; the Alu for the sake of &quot;making things more interesting&quot; like their peculiar deals with the Nhang as opposing the worms, if nor more so,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}